@startuml system-context
title HoneyComb Engine - Contexto del sistema
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Disenador" as designer
rectangle "Editor de niveles\nAngular + Electron" as editor
folder "Carpeta del editor\n(Documentos/HoneyComb por defecto)" as project {
  file "levels/*.json" as levels
  folder "assets/\ntextures, sounds" as assets
  file "characters.json\nitems.json" as libraries
}
folder "Instalacion de HoneyComb" as install {
  file "schema/level.schema.json\nschema/event_catalog.json" as schema
  file "engine.exe" as exe
}
rectangle "Runtime HoneyComb\nC++ + raylib" as runtime
actor "Jugador" as player

designer --> editor : crea y configura niveles
editor --> levels : lee / escribe
editor --> assets : copia imagenes y niveles\nde afuera (importar)
editor --> libraries : lee / escribe
editor --> schema : lee el catalogo de eventos
editor --> exe : Ejecutar (nivel por argumento)
exe --> runtime
runtime --> levels : carga nivel
runtime --> assets : carga texturas y sonidos\n({nivel}/../../assets)
player --> runtime : entrada y juego

note bottom of project
Contrato de integracion: JSON + assets en la carpeta
del editor. Todo lo que llega de afuera se COPIA
adentro; el original no se toca.
No existe comunicacion IPC en vivo entre
editor y runtime en esta version.
end note

note bottom of install
Los schemas son el CONTRATO entre los dos programas:
el editor tiene modelos TypeScript espejo de
level.schema.json, y el runtime implementa en C++
cada bloque de event_catalog.json. Son del programa,
no de cada proyecto.
end note
@enduml
